{"name":"Woodgrain","hex":"#996633","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodgrain","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The grain of wood.","The grained pattern of a wooden surface, especially as on a non-wooden object decorated as to appear wooden."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To texture a surface in imitation of the grain of wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodgrain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wood grain","blocks":[{"text":"Wood grain is the longitudinal arrangement of wood fibers or the pattern resulting from such an arrangement. It has various derived terms refer to different aspects of the fibers or patterns. Wood grain is important in woodworking and it impacts aesthetics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lodgepole_pine_spiral_grain.jpg/330px-Lodgepole_pine_spiral_grain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood_grain","wikidata":"Q1423948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Plain_quarter_sawn.png/330px-Plain_quarter_sawn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Plain_quarter_sawn.png/330px-Plain_quarter_sawn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketch of A—Quarter-sawn & B—flat-sawn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlain_quarter_sawn.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/RedGumTable.jpg/500px-RedGumTable.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/RedGumTable.jpg/500px-RedGumTable.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"typically figured red gum table","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedGumTable.jpg"},{"srcset":"h